@startuml
class User { -id: Long
-name: String
-email: String
-password: String
-role: Role }
enum Role { CUSTOMER
STAFF
ADMIN }
class Category { -categoryId: Long
-name: String
-description: String }
class Product { -productId: Long
-name: String
-price: BigDecimal
-quantity: Integer
-version: Long }
class Cart { -cartId: Long
-totalAmount: BigDecimal }
class CartItem { -cartItemId: Long
-quantity: Integer
-unitPrice: BigDecimal }
class Order { -orderId: Long
-orderDate: LocalDateTime
-totalAmount: BigDecimal
-status: OrderStatus
-checkoutKey: String }
class OrderItem { -orderItemId: Long
-quantity: Integer
-unitPrice: BigDecimal
-legacyPrice: BigDecimal }
enum OrderStatus { PENDING
CONFIRMED
PROCESSING
SHIPPED
DELIVERED
CANCELLED }
User --> Role
Category "1" <-- "0..*" Product
User "1" <-- "0..1" Cart
Cart "1" <-- "0..*" CartItem
Product "1" <-- "0..*" CartItem
User "1" <-- "0..*" Order
Order "1" <-- "1..*" OrderItem
Product "1" <-- "0..*" OrderItem
Order --> OrderStatus
note bottom
Domain diagram. Relationships do not claim JPA cascade deletion.
Controllers/services contain login, checkout and stock operations.
end note
@enduml
